Value vulnerabilities encompass every flavor of injection, data manipulation, and access flaw where the container holds data perfectly, but the application parses the data dangerously. [1] 
On platforms like [HackerOne](https://www.hackerone.com/bug-bounty-programs) or [Bugcrowd](https://help.doit.com/docs/vendor-information/bug-bounty-program), these are generally classified under the OWASP Top 10 rather than individual variables. Because corporate programs use the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) to calculate maximum impact, the cash payout depends entirely on whether the malicious value triggers a low-level error or a critical infrastructure compromise. [1, 2] 
