## Industry Realities Regarding Open Submissions
While corporate enterprise programs continue paying standard rates, be aware that major crowdsourced architectures have severely slashed open public baseline payouts. Platforms like Google and GitHub scaled back public open-submission fees due to massive influxes of AI-generated noise reports. GitHub, for instance, capped standard public critical findings much lower, restricting premium triple-rate tiers strictly to invite-only, vetted VIP groups. [15, 16] 
